jKanban is a simple desktop kanban board. Cards look like yellow
sticky notes and are dragged between columns. Work can be split into
up to 8 projects, each on its own tab.

Boards are saved automatically to
~/.local/share/com.jbernadas.jkanban/board.json. Removing the package
leaves them in place.

The second download is upstream's vendor tarball: the Rust crates the
program depends on, plus its prebuilt web interface. With it, the
build needs neither network access nor Node.js.

webkit2gtk4.1 and its dependencies take a long time to build.
